From 0376e5307e7fd2b19cd834def52e2aaa7e487388 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiro <chiro2001@163.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 18:56:57 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 250/258] perf(u2b): validate int8 codes in one bulk pass and
 stop leaking BLIS threads

verify-0042-u2b measured the per-element _check_codes isinstance loop at 20.7ms-5.06s of entry dispatch (op 0.29-2.61ms).  Replace it with a single array('b', values) conversion (C-level type/range work) plus one memchr for the reserved -128 code, and hand the converted buffers to the GEMM via prepare_int32(left_codes=..., right_codes=...) so the elements are marshalled once.  The strict per-element validator stays as the structured-error fallback for non-integer containers.  -128 and out-of-range remain fail-closed before any kernel call, outputs stay untouched, and the api_pinned path now restores BLIS's process-global thread count so it cannot leak into other providers.  Same-window evidence: dispatch geomean ~25x cheaper (1,1024,8192: 5.64s -> 157.5ms), leaving the unavoidable Python->C marshalling floor.
